InferenceService using the ROCm vLLM runtime deploys and serves on AMD\n  Instinct nodes through existing KServe machinery, with no KServe code\n  changes required (KServe is validated as-is).\n- The runtime's ROCm image baseline and driver prerequisites are recorded and\n  consistent with the versions the validation campaign certified.\n- The scope of productized models exactly matches the campaign's cleared-model\n  list; models that did not clear are documented as unsupported on ROCm.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Scope is bounded by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: the cleared\n  model list (partial, complete, or empty) rewrites this epic's scope, not its\n  structure.\n- Upstream ROCm runtime image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the\n  upstream communities and may not align with platform release trains; this is\n  a timing risk on the image baseline chosen, not a change in what is built.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34351,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96bb78b90d3832b2","agent_id":"a183521e810571ad7","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"f919c157-f843-4a86-ac9e-8e69c733bc48","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:56:29.415Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
