a-exhaustion and queueing behavior.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1, shared): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling —\n  this epic delivers the quota/admission half.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- On-hardware admission validation requires AMD Instinct nodes; where\n  hardware access is shared with the serving validation campaign, coordinate\n  scheduling — hardware availability is an external precondition, not a\n  deliverable condition.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34351,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96bb78b90d3832b2","agent_id":"a183521e810571ad7","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"2e674cb1-56e6-4e3e-820b-fba2532d37b8","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:56:35.815Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
