tion time — no rebuild of quota handling in this epic).\n- Validated PyTorch ROCm image baselines and job configuration patterns are\n  documented, with driver/ROCm versions recorded.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1, shared): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling —\n  this epic delivers the PyTorchJob training half.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Validation requires AMD Instinct nodes; where hardware access is shared with\n  the serving validation campaign, coordinate scheduling — hardware\n  availability is an external precondition, not a deliverable condition.\n- Upstream PyTorch ROCm image cadence is controlled by upstream communities\n  and AMD; the image baseline to validate against is a timing risk, not a\n  change in what is built.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34351,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96bb78b90d3832b2","agent_id":"a183521e810571ad7","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"52f8f994-c37f-40ee-90a3-98ae2b0a4b19","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:56:43.379Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
