{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1322cd7e55090e3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct vLLM serving validation campaign (functional/performance parity,\n4\t  go/no-go)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n6\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n7\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 0\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# AMD Instinct vLLM serving validation campaign (functional/performance parity, go/no-go)\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis epic resolves the central unknown of the AMD GPU (ROCm) enablement\n31\tstrategy: whether vLLM serving on AMD Instinct accelerators achieves\n32\tfunctional and performance parity with the platform's CUDA-based vLLM runtime\n33\tfor the supported model set. It runs a validation campaign on physical AMD\n34\tInstinct hardware, produces first-hand functional and performance parity data\n35\tper model, and delivers the go/no-go recommendation that bounds the scope of\n36\tthe vLLM ROCm serving-runtime productization work.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Secure access to dedicated AMD Instinct GPU nodes (procurement or partner-lab\n41\t  access) — the epic's work includes securing access; the timing of external\n42\t  granting is a risk, not a deliverable condition.\n43\t- Define the validation campaign methodology: the supported model set under\n44\t  test, functional pass/fail criteria per model, and performance parity\n45\t  measurement methodology against the CUDA baseline.\n46\t- Execute the campaign: run vLLM serving of the supported model set on ROCm on\n47\t  the AMD Instinct nodes, collecting functional results and performance\n48\t  metrics per model.\n49\t- Produce the validation report: per-model functional pass/fail, performance\n50\t  parity data, and the go/no-go recommendation with the list of models cleared\n51\t  for productization.\n52\t- Record driver and ROCm runtime versions used, so the productization and\n53\t  documentation work can reference validated configurations.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The validation campaign plan is documented and covers every model in the\n58\t  supported model set, with a defined functional pass/fail criterion and a\n59\t  defined performance parity measurement for each.\n60\t- Functional results exist for every model in the supported model set: each\n61\t  model is marked pass or fail against its criterion.\n62\t- Performance parity data is captured for every functionally passing model,\n63\t  measured against the CUDA vLLM baseline under the documented methodology.\n64\t- The validation report is published and states, per model: functional result,\n65\t  performance parity data, and driver/ROCm runtime versions used.\n66\t- The report delivers a go/no-go recommendation enumerating the models cleared\n67\t  for productization (the list may be empty, partial, or complete — the\n68\t  deliverable is the decision data, not a particular outcome).\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (P0): A validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n73\t  establishes functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n74\t  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- Hardware access is an availability precondition controlled by parties\n79\t  outside the strategy (procurement or partner-lab negotiation); its timing\n80\t  cannot be compressed by engineering effort and gates campaign execution.\n81\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image cadence is controlled by AMD and upstream\n82\t  communities; the campaign should pin and record the versions it validates.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b47f6c2c089dde6","agent_id":"a057933bc08afe678","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"77172e4c-ec31-4b96-aa92-ee862c07649c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:58:29.578Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1322cd7e55090e3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
