{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb949ce6be2435b1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n3\ttitle: Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling and admission for ROCm workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue amd.com/gpu quota handling and admission for ROCm workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic enables the Distributed Workloads stack's queueing layer to admit\n34\tworkloads requesting AMD Instinct GPUs: `amd.com/gpu` resource quota handling\n35\tin the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue model, and all-or-nothing (gang)\n36\tadmission of multi-GPU ROCm jobs onto AMD GPU nodes.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Extend the quota/admission configuration model of the Distributed Workloads\n41\t  stack so ClusterQueues/LocalQueues can meter and limit `amd.com/gpu`\n42\t  resources, mirroring how NVIDIA GPU quota is handled today.\n43\t- Ensure resource flavors can target AMD Instinct node pools so queued\n44\t  workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` admit onto the right nodes.\n45\t- Verify all-or-nothing admission (gang semantics via waitForPodsReady) for\n46\t  multi-GPU and multi-node ROCm job topologies.\n47\t- Validate admission behavior with representative queued workloads requesting\n48\t  `amd.com/gpu` (single-GPU and multi-GPU), including quota exhaustion and\n49\t  queueing behavior.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration meters and enforces quota on\n54\t  `amd.com/gpu`, and workloads exceeding quota remain pending rather than\n55\t  admitting.\n56\t- Workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted onto AMD Instinct node\n57\t  pools, with correct resource accounting per admitted workload.\n58\t- Multi-GPU/multi-node ROCm job topologies admit all-or-nothing: partial\n59\t  topologies do not admit, and released quota is reclaimed when workloads\n60\t  finish.\n61\t- Admission validation results for single- and multi-GPU ROCm workloads are\n62\t  documented, including quota-exhaustion and queueing behavior.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1, shared): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n67\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling —\n68\t  this epic delivers the quota/admission half.\n69\t\n70\t## Risks / Notes\n71\t\n72\t- On-hardware admission validation requires AMD Instinct nodes; where\n73\t  hardware access is shared with the serving validation campaign, coordinate\n74\t  scheduling — hardware availability is an external precondition, not a\n75\t  deliverable condition.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b47f6c2c089dde6","agent_id":"a057933bc08afe678","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"49ad7353-7aec-4b5a-8926-981c91e4369d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:58:30.851Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb949ce6be2435b1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
