{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-974c786026567866","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9020\n3\tscore: 12\n4\tpass: false\n5\trecommendation: revise\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: major\n8\t  criterion: Type Correctness\n9\t  description: 'E005 lists the Investigation epic RHAISTRAT-9020-E001 in its dependencies\n10\t    but has gated_by: null — the campaign outcome (cleared/failed model list, including\n11\t    models documented as unsupported on ROCm) rewrites the content scope of E005,\n12\t    so the dependency is a true gate. Fix: set gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9020-E001 with gate_failure_impact\n13\t    (action: rewrite, fallback: document the failed-model list / no-models-supported\n14\t    outcome), or drop the direct edge only if the model-list content is consumed transitively\n15\t    via E002.'\n16\terror: null\n17\t---\n18\t## Review Summary\n19\t\n20\tScore: 12/14 — fail\n21\tRecommendation: revise\n22\t\n23\tcontract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-9020` exits 0 — body\n24\tsections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority\n25\tinheritance, and implementation-type parallelism all pass). Triage consistency:\n26\t`triage: null` (full decomposition) with 5 epics — multi-epic output is expected,\n27\tno Step 1.5 contradiction. One major gating-metadata defect found in Type\n28\tCorrectness; all other criteria pass clean.\n29\t\n30\t## Criterion Details\n31\t\n32\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n33\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1 (P0) → E001, HLR-2 (P0) → E002, HLR-3 (P1) →\n34\tE003 + E004, HLR-4 (P2) → E005. Priority inheritance is correct: E001 (P0) gates\n35\tonly P0 work (E002); E003/E004 (P1) block only E005, whose priority derives from\n36\tthe docs-authoring exception (strategy `priority: Major` → P1), not from the\n37\timplementations it depends on. The HLR-3 split is by component boundary (Kueue\n38\tquota/admission vs. Training Operator PyTor