1\t- How to run PyTorch training on ROCm: single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n52\t  admitted through Kueue with `amd.com/gpu` quota, using the validated job\n53\t  configuration patterns.\n54\t- Scope boundaries carried over from the strategy: non-AMD accelerator\n55\t  families and AMD GPU sharing/partitioning are out of scope and documented as\n56\t  unsupported.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Documentation topics covering supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites,\n61\t  the validated model list for serving, and ROCm training configuration are\n62\t  authored and published through the Red Hat docs content process.\n63\t- The documented validated model list matches the productized runtime's\n64\t  supported model set exactly.\n65\t- The documented driver/ROCm prerequisites match the versions validated on\n66\t  hardware and shipped in the productized runtime.\n67\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented and validated\n68\t  behavior (reviewed by the owning engineers of the serving runtime and\n69\t  training stack).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n74\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- Documentation content depends on the outcomes of the validation campaign,\n79\t  runtime productization, and training enablement; it is scheduled after all\n80\t  implementation work by design.\n81\t- Epic priority is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n82\t  frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1); the HLR's P2 label reads as relative\n83\t  value, not a deferral signal.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9771db83a6f0ef4d","agent_id":"a9fb23f5099235ee4","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"01097d8e-42b7-4b24-b3f8-9c5a14d22ddb","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:01:41.660Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f9c286b54582d49","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept",