{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92b38f2b49d9237c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Document AMD hardware support, driver prerequisites, and validated model list\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n14\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n15\tai_signals:\n16\t  change_specificity: 1\n17\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n18\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n19\t  existing_foundation: 1\n20\t  open_questions: 1\n21\t  external_dependency: 0\n22\t  human_process_gates: -1\n23\t  repo_access: 1\n24\t  architecture_claims: 0\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 4\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n31\tgate_failure_impact:\n32\t  action: rewrite\n33\t  fallback_approach: 'The documentation epic exists whatever the campaign outcome:\n34\t    the documented validated model list rewrites with the campaign result — models\n35\t    that did not clear (up to and including a no-models-supported outcome) are documented\n36\t    as unsupported on ROCm, and the driver/hardware prerequisites reflect the versions\n37\t    actually validated.'\n38\t---\n39\t# Document AMD hardware support, driver prerequisites, and validated model list\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tThis epic authors the customer-facing documentation for AMD GPU (ROCm)\n44\tenablement: the supported AMD Instinct hardware, driver prerequisites, and the\n45\tvalidated model list for vLLM ROCm serving (plus the validated PyTorch ROCm\n46\ttraining configuration), reflecting what was actually built and validated.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Supported AMD Instinct accelerators and the hardware requirements for both\n51\t  serving and training on ROCm.\n52\t- Driver and ROCm runtime prerequisites, including the validated driver/ROCm\n53\t  versions recorded by the validation campaign and productization work.\n54\t- The validated model list for vLLM ROCm serving — exactly the models the\n55\t  validation campaign cleared and the productized runtime supports — with\n56\t  models that did not clear explicitly documented as unsupported on ROCm.\n57\t- How to run PyTorch training on ROCm: single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJobs\n58\t  admitted through Kueue with `amd.com/gpu` quota, using the validated job\n59\t  configuration patterns.\n60\t- Scope boundaries carried over from the strategy: non-AMD accelerator\n61\t  families and AMD GPU sharing/partitioning are out of scope and documented as\n62\t  unsupported.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- Documentation topics covering supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites,\n67\t  the validated model list for serving, and ROCm training configuration are\n68\t  authored and published through the Red Hat docs content process.\n69\t- The documented validated model list matches the productized runtime's\n70\t  supported model set exactly.\n71\t- The documented driver/ROCm prerequisites match the versions validated on\n72\t  hardware and shipped in the productized runtime.\n73\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented and validated\n74\t  behavior (reviewed by the owning engineers of the serving runtime and\n75\t  training stack).\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- HLR-4 (P2): Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver\n80\t  prerequisites, and the validated model list.\n81\t\n82\t## Risks / Notes\n83\t\n84\t- Documentation content depends on the outcomes of the validation campaign,\n85\t  runtime productization, and training enablement; it is scheduled after all\n86\t  implementation work by design.\n87\t- Epic priority is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n88\t  frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1); the HLR's P2 label reads as relative\n89\t  value, not a deferral signal.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9bc615150bc042b","agent_id":"a4fc28b42d7daf7b3","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"1751ef4e-56aa-4feb-b614-55d1427ef726","timestamp":"2026-10-23T21:28:46.185Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92b38f2b49d9237c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
