{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a018f99a36b4bc5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n3\ttitle: Productize vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the campaign clears fewer or no models, the productization\n15\t    scope shrinks to the cleared subset or is not undertaken; the epic structure is\n16\t    unchanged and only the model list is rewritten.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Productize vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic productizes a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the models\n39\tcleared by the AMD Instinct validation campaign, extending the platform's\n40\tServing Runtimes portfolio (currently CUDA-only) with an AMD Instinct\n41\tvariant. The runtime must be deployable through the existing KServe\n42\tInferenceService machinery and built through the existing runtime build and\n43\trelease pipeline.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Build and productize vLLM ROCm runtime images for the models cleared by the\n48\t  validation campaign, based on the ROCm baseline validated in the campaign.\n49\t- Define and ship the ServingRuntime/ClusterServingRuntime resources that make\n50\t  the ROCm vLLM runtime selectable for inference on AMD Instinct nodes.\n51\t- Ensure the runtime integrates with accelerator discovery on AMD GPU nodes so\n52\t  InferenceServices using this runtime schedule onto AMD Instinct nodes.\n53\t- Validate deployment through KServe InferenceServices (serverless and/or raw\n54\t  deployment mode as supported) without KServe code changes — KServe\n55\t  compatibility is verified here, not modified.\n56\t- Align the runtime's ROCm image baseline with platform release trains,\n57\t  subject to upstream ROCm image availability.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A vLLM ROCm serving runtime image builds successfully through the existing\n62\t  runtime build pipeline (pipeline green) for every model on the campaign's\n63\t  cleared list.\n64\t- The runtime is selectable via ServingRuntime resources and serves every\n65\t  cleared model with functional behavior matching the campaign's validated\n66\t  results.\n67\t- An InferenceService using the ROCm vLLM runtime deploys and serves on AMD\n68\t  Instinct nodes through existing KServe machinery, with no KServe code\n69\t  changes required (KServe is validated as-is).\n70\t- The runtime's ROCm image baseline and driver prerequisites are recorded and\n71\t  consistent with the versions the validation campaign certified.\n72\t- The scope of productized models exactly matches the campaign's cleared-model\n73\t  list; models that did not clear are documented as unsupported on ROCm.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-2 (P0): A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the\n78\t  models the validation campaign clears.\n79\t\n80\t## Risks / Notes\n81\t\n82\t- Scope is bounded by the validation campaign's go/no-go outcome: the cleared\n83\t  model list (partial, complete, or empty) rewrites this epic's scope, not its\n84\t  structure.\n85\t- Upstream ROCm runtime image release cadence is controlled by AMD and the\n86\t  upstream communities and may not align with platform release trains; this is\n87\t  a timing risk on the image baseline chosen, not a change in what is built.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84b4c1ca4ccae2d6","agent_id":"a6348c406ab172fa5","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"a3706c95-dede-4cc0-a657-2efb693d364a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:35:42.215Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a018f99a36b4bc5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Retry re-review of RHAISTRAT-9020"}
