{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-839e2e7435a6a78d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: PyTorchJob ROCm training support (single- and multi-GPU)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorchJob ROCm training support (single- and multi-GPU)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes PyTorch distributed training on AMD Instinct GPUs a supported\n34\tpath: PyTorchJob workloads running ROCm-based PyTorch training images, in\n35\tsingle- and multi-GPU topologies, admitted through Kueue with `amd.com/gpu`\n36\tquota handling.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Enable PyTorchJob workers to run ROCm-based PyTorch training images on AMD\n41\t  Instinct nodes, including the worker/launcher configuration needed for\n42\t  single-GPU and multi-GPU (multi-node) topologies.\n43\t- Validate end-to-end training: PyTorchJobs admitted through Kueue queues\n44\t  configured for `amd.com/gpu`, executing training runs on ROCm — the quota\n45\t  configuration itself is delivered by the Distributed Workloads stack and is\n46\t  consumed here as a configuration reference, not rebuilt.\n47\t- Document validated PyTorch ROCm image baselines and job configuration\n48\t  patterns for single- and multi-GPU training.\n49\t- Capture validation results (functional training runs, scaling behavior\n50\t  across single/multi-GPU) on AMD Instinct hardware.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A single-GPU PyTorchJob running a ROCm PyTorch training image completes a\n55\t  training run on an AMD Instinct node, admitted through a Kueue queue\n56\t  metering `amd.com/gpu`.\n57\t- A multi-GPU PyTorchJob (multi-worker and/or multi-GPU-per-worker topology)\n58\t  completes a distributed training run on AMD Instinct nodes with the same\n59\t  admission path.\n60\t- End-to-end validation is performed against Kueue queues configured for\n61\t  `amd.com/gpu` (the quota configuration is available as a configuration\n62\t  reference at validation time — no rebuild of quota handling in this epic).\n63\t- Validated PyTorch ROCm image baselines and job configuration patterns are\n64\t  documented, with driver/ROCm versions recorded.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-3 (P1, shared): PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and\n69\t  multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling —\n70\t  this epic delivers the PyTorchJob training half.\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Validation requires AMD Instinct nodes; where hardware access is shared with\n75\t  the serving validation campaign, coordinate scheduling — hardware\n76\t  availability is an external precondition, not a deliverable condition.\n77\t- Upstream PyTorch ROCm image cadence is controlled by upstream communities\n78\t  and AMD; the image baseline to validate against is a timing risk, not a\n79\t  change in what is built.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84b4c1ca4ccae2d6","agent_id":"a6348c406ab172fa5","session_id":"1dade12c-3f35-491e-b719-6185ca00038a","uuid":"235375dc-5f91-42af-85f2-8ca128611764","timestamp":"2026-10-24T06:35:46.968Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-839e2e7435a6a78d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Retry